From 57197d34a4230224306d3ed0b6dcaa40a266cd0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:27:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sim): a chamfer or deburr owns its declared edge break

The program sim judged the bevel a 2D Chamfer or Deburr exists to cut
against the model's sharp edge, so the post gate refused every one.

The chamfer and deburr generators now declare the break they were asked
to cut (cl::EdgeBreak: the edge, the bevel depth and slope from the op's
own parameters, not from the moves). After deviate, the program sim
re-judges a gouge column inside a declared break's width against the
bevel: down to it is clean, deeper is still a gouge charged at its
excess, and an undeclared edge keeps the model's verdict. The record
persists as an additive `breaks` key in the cached path.

The deburr also stops riding edges steeper than its cone's flank: a
vertical cone on a vertical corner countersank it to the window floor
(9.8 mm on the default brick), a real gouge. It skips them with a note.

Fixes #303

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
